      "description": "Each line is one whole ZFS backing disk, labeled by host and device. rate(read/write time) / rate(completed operations), with no host or cluster aggregation. No completed operations means no latency sample. Linux block-request mean latency, not application latency or a percentile. Legend Max is the highest displayed interval mean within the selected time range, not the slowest individual I/O.",
